+# Acoustic Forensics: Forensic Evaluation & Verification Dossier
+**Project**: Acoustic Forensics / VeriVox (Synthetic Speech & Deepfake Audio Detection)  
+**System Version**: 2.4.0 (Pipeline Verification Phase)  
+**Author/Team**: Antigravity Machine Learning & Audio Forensics Engineering  
+**Evaluation Standard**: Smoke-Test Pipeline Verification (Real ASVspoof 2019 LA Evaluation In Progress)  
+**Date of Evaluation**: November 2026  
+
+---
+
+> [!WARNING]
+> **FORMAL RETRACTION & SCIENTIFIC AUDIT NOTICE**  
+> Prior iterations of this dossier reported headline metrics (such as 0.0000% EER, 1.0000 ROC-AUC, and 98% "In-the-Wild" accuracy). A rigorous scientific review identified that these results were generated exclusively against a mock synthetic smoke-test dataset (`data/smoke_test`, generated by `scripts/prepare_data.py::generate_smoke_test_dataset` with synthetic sine wave harmonics and injected high-frequency test tones) for end-to-end integration testing.  
+>
+> **All claims of "Official ASVspoof 2019 LA evaluation", "0% EER", "98% In-the-Wild accuracy", "unseen attacks A07–A19", and "production readiness" have been formally RETRACTED.**  
+>
+> The mock outputs have been moved to `results_smoke/`. All active evaluation pipelines now strictly enforce cryptographic provenance tracking (`dataset_name`, `manifest_sha256`, `git_commit`, `seed`, `timestamp`), zero-leakage speaker disjointness, and smoke-test guards. Genuine scientific evaluation on the complete ASVspoof 2019 Logical Access dataset (25,380 train, 24,844 dev, 71,237 eval trials) and external In-the-Wild dataset is underway.
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+This dossier documents the pipeline verification benchmarks of **Acoustic Forensics**, an end-to-end machine learning system developed to distinguish authentic human speech (*bona fide*) from synthetic speech and voice conversion deepfakes (*spoof*) at 16 kHz audio resolution.
+
+### Sanity Verification Metrics on Mock Smoke Data (`results_smoke/`):
+- **Stacked Ensemble (L2 Meta-Learner)**:
+  - **Smoke Equal Error Rate (EER)**: `0.0000%` (Sanity check on synthetic mock signals only)
+  - **Smoke Area Under ROC Curve (ROC-AUC)**: `1.0000`
+  - **Smoke Minimum Tandem Detection Cost Function (min-tDCF)**: `0.0000`
+- **Notice on Real Benchmark Evaluation**:
+  - Genuine evaluations on official ASVspoof 2019 LA splits are pending execution in STAGE 1–STAGE 8.
+
+### Production Readiness Verdict
+**Status: NOT READY (Smoke-Test Pipeline Checks Only; Real Dataset Evaluation In Progress)**  
+- *Justification 1*: Headline separation was measured only on mock synthetic signals (`data/smoke_test`). Evaluation on real human phonation and unseen vocoders (A07–A19) has not yet been conducted.
+- *Justification 2*: Provenance tracking and speaker disjointness audits have been put in place (STAGE 0); real data downloads and verified protocols are required before deployment.
+- *Justification 3*: Production deployment requires verified baseline reproduction, fair feature comparison, and out-of-fold calibrated fusion.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Problem Definition & Evaluation Framework
+
+### 2.1 Task Formulation
+- **Classification Objective**: Given a single-channel audio recording $x \in \mathbb{R}^N$ sampled at 16,000 Hz, predict the posterior probability $P(y = 1 \mid x) \in [0, 1]$, where:
+  - $y = 1$: **Bona Fide** (Authentic human phonation recorded through a physical microphone).
+  - $y = 0$: **Spoof** (Synthetic speech generated via text-to-speech vocoders or voice conversion algorithms).
+- **Secondary Objective**: Compute a frame-level temporal attention salience vector $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}^T$ indicating which phonetic frames drove the classification decision.
+
+### 2.2 Biometric & Forensic Metrics
+1. **Equal Error Rate (EER)**: The operating threshold where the False Acceptance Rate ($\text{FAR} = \text{FP} / (\text{FP} + \text{TN})$) equals the False Rejection Rate ($\text{FRR} = \text{FN} / (\text{FN} + \text{TP})$).
+2. **ROC-AUC & PR-AUC**: Area under the Receiver Operating Characteristic and Precision-Recall curves.
+3. **Minimum Tandem Detection Cost Function (min-tDCF)**: The official ASVspoof metric evaluating the countermeasure operating in tandem with an automatic speaker verification (ASV) system:
+   $$\text{tDCF}(s) = C_{\text{miss}} \cdot P_{\text{tar}} \cdot P_{\text{miss}}^{\text{cm}}(s) + C_{\text{fa}} \cdot P_{\text{non}} \cdot \frac{P_{\text{fa}}^{\text{asv}}}{1 - P_{\text{miss}}^{\text{asv}}} + C_{\text{fa}} \cdot P_{\text{spoof}} \cdot P_{\text{fa}}^{\text{cm}}(s)$$
+   Parameters: $P_{\text{tar}} = 0.05, P_{\text{non}} = 0.05, P_{\text{spoof}} = 0.90, C_{\text{miss}} = 1.0, C_{\text{fa}} = 10.0$.
+4. **Sign Convention**: Continuous score $s \in (-\infty, +\infty)$ where higher values indicate bona fide speech ($s > \theta \implies \text{Genuine}$).
+
+---
